{
  "config": {
    "step": {
      "user": {
        "title": "Personal Weather Station",
        "description": "Set a station key here that your weather stations must transmit so that their data is not rejected. If you leave the field blank, all requests will be accepted.",
        "data": {
          "password": "Station key"
        }
      }
    },
    "abort": {
      "single_instance_allowed": "Already configured. A single instance serves every weather station."
    }
  },
  "options": {
    "step": {
      "init": {
        "title": "Personal Weather Station",
        "menu_options": {
          "options": "Settings",
          "instructions": "How to point a station at Home Assistant"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "issues": {
    "invalid_station_key": {
      "title": "Weather station rejected: wrong station key",
      "description": "A weather station at {ip} tried to send data as `{station_id}` but did not send the expected station key.\n\nCheck that the station key configured in the station or in the WSLink app matches the one set in this integration. This message disappears on its own once a request from {ip} is accepted."
    },
    "missing_device_id": {
      "title": "Weather station rejected: no station identifier",
      "description": "A weather station at {ip} sent data without a station identifier.\n\nSet a Sender ID in the WSLink app, or an ID parameter in the station configuration. This message disappears on its own once a request from {ip} is accepted."
    },
    "legacy_entity_ids": {
      "title": "Entity IDs repeat the station name",
      "fix_flow": {
        "step": {
          "confirm": {
            "title": "Shorten the entity IDs",
            "description": "Up to version 1.0.8 this integration built entity IDs that carry the station name twice, such as `{example_old}`. New stations no longer do.\n\n**{count} entities** can be renamed, for example to `{example_new}`.\n\nHistory and long-term statistics follow the rename automatically. **Automations, scripts, scenes and dashboards do not** — you will have to update anything that refers to the old IDs yourself.\n\nIf you would rather keep them as they are, ignore this repair."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "legacy_status_sensors": {
      "title": "Connection, leak and battery readings are still numbers",
      "fix_flow": {
        "step": {
          "confirm": {
            "title": "Convert to binary sensors",
            "description": "Connection, water leak and battery readings are reported as 1 or 0. Up to version 1.0.8 they were exposed as numeric sensors, such as `{example}`, which cannot be used with the standard leak, connectivity and low-battery cards of Home Assistant. New stations get binary sensors showing **Wet / Dry**, **Connected / Disconnected** and **On / Off**.\n\n**{count} entities** can be converted. The 0~5 battery levels of the air quality sensors keep their percentage: six steps are more than an on/off can carry.\n\nChanging platform is not a rename, so the old entities are removed and rebuilt as `binary_sensor`. **Their recorded history is lost** — these readings have no long-term statistics, so only the raw history is affected — and **automations, scripts, scenes and dashboards pointing at them must be updated**. The new entities appear on the station's next upload.\n\nIf you would rather keep them as they are, ignore this repair."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "unknown_parameters": {
      "title": "Station {station} is sending readings that are being dropped",
      "description": "**{count} parameters** from **{station}** are not recognised, so their values are discarded on every upload:\n\n{parameters}\n\nThe usual cause is a station reporting more than its protocol can carry. Weather Underground has only **4 slots** for extra sensors; if your station offers **WSLink** as an *API type*, switching to it exposes seven channels and roughly twice as many readings.\n\nIf that is not it, these parameter names are exactly what a bug report needs: open one on the [issue tracker]({issue_tracker}) and they can be added.\n\nYou can also ignore this — nothing is broken, these particular values simply do not arrive."
    }
  },
